<title>UK: Connex trains cancelled as UK drivers take action.</title>
<headline>Connex trains cancelled as UK drivers take action.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Twenty percent of trains run by Connex South Central, part of Cie Generale des Eaux, will be cancelled on Friday because of industrial action by drivers, the company said.</p>
<p>Connex operates services out of London's Victoria and London Bridge stations to Sussex, Surrey and Hampshire. It said 334 trains will be cancelled because of an overtime ban by members of the drivers' union Aslef.</p>
<p>A further 116 trains will be cancelled for part of their journey.</p>
<p>The disruption will be worse on Saturday when 435 trains will be cancelled - 30 percent of the total - and a further 179 will not complete their normal journeys.</p>
<p>-- London newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
